# A-box check: catalogue as yardstick. The qualities of clause 3.5 are supplied
# as named individuals and the answer reports, per quality, whether the case
# states a value for it. Without a case every one reads as not stated, which is
# what the question asks rather than an answer from the pattern.
#
# CQ 26: Which qualities of the catalogue does a case state a value for, and
# which does it leave open?
#
# Clause 3.5 defines the qualities of a trustworthy AI system, robustness,
# reliability, transparency and the rest, and they are supplied as named
# individuals. A model states a value for as many as it can support.
#
# Listing them would report the same nine whatever case is loaded. Holding them
# against the case reports what this system actually claims about itself, and
# the unstated half is the half a review asks about: a system with no stated
# robustness has not said how it behaves outside its training distribution.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
SELECT ?quality ?standing ?holder ?quantity ?unit
WHERE {
  ?q a iso:VariableCharacteristic .
  OPTIONAL {
    ?value iso:forCharacteristic ?q .
    OPTIONAL { ?holder iso:hasCharacteristicValue ?value }
    OPTIONAL { ?value iso:quantity ?quantity }
    OPTIONAL { ?value iso:unit     ?unit }
  }
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?value), "stated", "not stated") AS ?standing)
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?q), ".*#", "") AS ?quality)
} ORDER BY ?standing ?quality
